    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 155.2,
      "durationSeconds": 3.2,
      "text": "average."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 156.56,
      "durationSeconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Another example, for a ride-sharing"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 158.4,
      "durationSeconds": 6.76,
      "text": "service like Uber, weekend nights could"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 161.68,
      "durationSeconds": 5.64,
      "text": "have twice as many riders as average."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 165.16,
      "durationSeconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Now, let's go over an example. We'll"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 167.32,
      "durationSeconds": 3.92,
      "text": "estimate the number of tweets created"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 169.44,
      "durationSeconds": 3.92,
      "text": "per second on Twitter."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 171.24,
      "durationSeconds": 4.64,
      "text": "Note, these numbers are made up and they"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 173.36,
      "durationSeconds": 5.76,
      "text": "are not official numbers from Twitter."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 175.88,
      "durationSeconds": 6.16,
      "text": "Let's assume Twitter has 300 million MAU"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 179.12,
      "durationSeconds": 6.32,
      "text": "and 50% of the MAU use Twitter daily."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 182.04,
      "durationSeconds": 6.4,
      "text": "So, that's about 150 million DAU."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 185.44,
      "durationSeconds": 5.4,
      "text": "Next, we estimate that about 25% of"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 188.44,
      "durationSeconds": 4.96,
      "text": "Twitter DAU make tweets."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 190.84,
      "durationSeconds": 4.04,
      "text": "And each one on average makes two"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 193.4,
      "durationSeconds": 5.32,
      "text": "tweets."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 194.88,
      "durationSeconds": 5.4,
      "text": "That is 25% * 2, so it is 0.5 tweets per"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 198.72,
      "durationSeconds": 3.88,
      "text": "DAU."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 200.28,
      "durationSeconds": 4.92,
      "text": "For the scaling factor, we estimate that"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 202.6,
      "durationSeconds": 4.52,
      "text": "most people tweet in the morning when"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 205.2,
      "durationSeconds": 4.16,
      "text": "they get up and can't wait to share what"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 207.12,
      "durationSeconds": 4.44,
      "text": "they dream about the night before. And"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 209.36,
      "durationSeconds": 4.879,
      "text": "that spikes the tweet created per"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 211.56,
      "durationSeconds": 5.2,
      "text": "traffic to twice the average when the US"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 214.239,
      "durationSeconds": 4.041,
      "text": "East Coast wakes up, let's say."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 216.76,
      "durationSeconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Now, we have enough to calculate the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 218.28,
      "durationSeconds": 8.72,
      "text": "peak tweets created per second. We have"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 221.56,
      "durationSeconds": 9.72,
      "text": "150 million DAU * 0.5 tweets per DAU * 2"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 227,
      "durationSeconds": 6.32,
      "text": "times scaling factor divided by 86,400"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 231.28,
      "durationSeconds": 4.44,
      "text": "seconds in a day."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 233.32,
      "durationSeconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Now, that is roughly about 1,500 tweets"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 235.72,
      "durationSeconds": 3.92,
      "text": "created per second."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 237.6,
      "durationSeconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Let's go over the techniques we used to"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 239.64,
      "durationSeconds": 4.6,
      "text": "simplify the calculations."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 241.88,
      "durationSeconds": 4.28,
      "text": "First, we convert all big numbers to"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 244.24,
      "durationSeconds": 4.28,
      "text": "scientific notation."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 246.16,
      "durationSeconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Doing math on really big numbers is very"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 248.52,
      "durationSeconds": 3.439,
      "text": "error-prone."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 249.8,
      "durationSeconds": 4.56,
      "text": "By converting big numbers to scientific"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 251.959,
      "durationSeconds": 5.56,
      "text": "notation, part of the multiplication"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 254.36,
      "durationSeconds": 4.879,
      "text": "becomes simple addition, and division"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 257.519,
      "durationSeconds": 4.961,
      "text": "becomes subtraction."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 259.239,
      "durationSeconds": 9.561,
      "text": "In the example above, 150 million DAU"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 262.48,
      "durationSeconds": 9.64,
      "text": "becomes 150 * 10 ^ 6 or 1.5 * 10 ^ 8."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 268.8,
      "durationSeconds": 5.96,
      "text": "There are 86,400 seconds in a day. We"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 272.12,
      "durationSeconds": 5.48,
      "text": "round it up to 100,000 seconds, and that"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 274.76,
      "durationSeconds": 5.2,
      "text": "becomes 10 ^ 5 seconds."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 277.6,
      "durationSeconds": 5.76,
      "text": "And since it's a division, 10 ^ 5"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 279.96,
      "durationSeconds": 5.36,
      "text": "becomes 10 ^ -5."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 283.36,
      "durationSeconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Next, we group all the power of 10s"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 285.32,
      "durationSeconds": 3.68,
      "text": "together,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 286.44,
      "durationSeconds": 7.8,
      "text": "and then all other numbers together."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 289,
      "durationSeconds": 10.52,
      "text": "So, the math becomes 1.5 * 0.5 * 2,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 294.24,
      "durationSeconds": 10,
      "text": "and uh 10 ^ 8 * 10 ^ -5, which is equal"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 299.52,
      "durationSeconds": 7.72,
      "text": "to 10 ^ 8 - 5, which is 10 ^ 3."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 304.24,
      "durationSeconds": 6.16,
      "text": "Putting all together is like 1.5 * 10 ^"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 307.24,
      "durationSeconds": 4.92,
      "text": "3 or 1,500."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 310.4,
      "durationSeconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Now, with practice, we should be able to"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 312.16,
      "durationSeconds": 4.2,
      "text": "convert a large number to a scientific"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 314.24,
      "durationSeconds": 3.92,
      "text": "notation in seconds."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 316.36,
      "durationSeconds": 3.32,
      "text": "And here are some handy conversions we"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 318.16,
      "durationSeconds": 3.92,
      "text": "should memorize."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 319.68,
      "durationSeconds": 4.36,
      "text": "As an example, we should know by heart"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 322.08,
      "durationSeconds": 5.04,
      "text": "that 10 ^ 12"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 324.04,
      "durationSeconds": 5.44,
      "text": "is a trillion or a terabyte. And when we"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 327.12,
      "durationSeconds": 4.96,
      "text": "see a number like 50 terabyte, we should"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 329.48,
      "durationSeconds": 6.8,
      "text": "be able to convert it quickly to 50 * 10"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 332.08,
      "durationSeconds": 5.839,
      "text": "^ 12, which is 5 * 10 ^ 13."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 336.28,
      "durationSeconds": 4.52,
      "text": "We're going to ignore the fact that 1"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 337.919,
      "durationSeconds": 6.881,
      "text": "kilobyte is actually 2 ^ 10 bytes or"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 340.8,
      "durationSeconds": 6.2,
      "text": "1,024 bytes, and not a dozen bytes. We"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 344.8,
      "durationSeconds": 4.36,
      "text": "don't need the that degree of accuracy"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 347,
      "durationSeconds": 3.92,
      "text": "for back of the envelope math."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 349.16,
      "durationSeconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Now, let's wrap up by going through one"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 350.92,
      "durationSeconds": 4.96,
      "text": "last example. We'll estimate how much"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 353.44,
      "durationSeconds": 5.36,
      "text": "storage is required for storing"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 355.88,
      "durationSeconds": 5,
      "text": "multimedia files for tweets."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 358.8,
      "durationSeconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Now, we know from previous example that"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 360.88,
      "durationSeconds": 3.16,
      "text": "there are about 150 million tweets per"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 363.12,
      "durationSeconds": 3.68,
      "text": "day."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 364.04,
      "durationSeconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Now, we need an estimate on a percentage"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 366.8,
      "durationSeconds": 5.2,
      "text": "of tweets that could contain multimedia"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 368.84,
      "durationSeconds": 4.96,
      "text": "content and how large those files are on"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 372,
      "durationSeconds": 4.4,
      "text": "average."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 373.8,
      "durationSeconds": 5.76,
      "text": "From meticulous research, we estimate"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 376.4,
      "durationSeconds": 6.36,
      "text": "that 10% of tweets contain pictures and"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 379.56,
      "durationSeconds": 5.48,
      "text": "they're about 100 kilobyte each and 1%"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 382.76,
      "durationSeconds": 4.68,
      "text": "of all the tweets contain videos and"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 385.04,
      "durationSeconds": 4.6,
      "text": "they're about 100 megabyte each. We"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 387.44,
      "durationSeconds": 4.8,
      "text": "further assume that the files are"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 389.64,
      "durationSeconds": 5.2,
      "text": "replicated with three copies each and"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 392.24,
      "durationSeconds": 3.64,
      "text": "that Twitter would keep the media for 5"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 394.84,
      "durationSeconds": 2.92,
      "text": "years."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 395.88,
      "durationSeconds": 4.48,
      "text": "Now, here's the math. For storing"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 397.76,
      "durationSeconds": 5.4,
      "text": "pictures, we have the following."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 400.36,
      "durationSeconds": 5.36,
      "text": "We have 150 million tweets times one in"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 403.16,
      "durationSeconds": 5.64,
      "text": "10 tweets with pictures times 100"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 405.72,
      "durationSeconds": 6.84,
      "text": "kilobyte per picture times 400 days in a"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 408.8,
      "durationSeconds": 7.04,
      "text": "year times 5 years times three copies."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 412.56,
      "durationSeconds": 7,
      "text": "So, that turns into 1.5 times 10 to the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 415.84,
      "durationSeconds": 6.96,
      "text": "eighth times 10 to the minus one times"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 419.56,
      "durationSeconds": 6.76,
      "text": "10 to the fifth times four times 10 to"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 422.8,
      "durationSeconds": 5.16,
      "text": "the second times five times three."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 426.32,
      "durationSeconds": 5.52,
      "text": "Again, we group the powers of 10s"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 427.96,
      "durationSeconds": 7.44,
      "text": "together. This becomes 1.5 times four"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 431.84,
      "durationSeconds": 7.64,
      "text": "times five times three, which is 90."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 435.4,
      "durationSeconds": 7.4,
      "text": "And 10 to the eighth minus one plus five"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 439.48,
      "durationSeconds": 6.24,
      "text": "plus two, which is 10 to the 14th. And"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 442.8,
      "durationSeconds": 6.84,
      "text": "that becomes 90 times 10 to the 15,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 445.72,
      "durationSeconds": 6.04,
      "text": "which is from the table 9 petabytes."
    },
    {
